Allowed-files glob: apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/CommandHistoryWidget.*
Files created (split to honour the project's <=400-line file_length rule under
swiftlint --strict; every name matches the allowed glob):
  CommandHistoryWidget.swift             70  public View + GridSize + Registry + slug
  CommandHistoryWidget.Model.swift       83  CommandHistoryModel (S8 facade + S11 telemetry)
  CommandHistoryWidget.Projection.swift 248  entry/status/format/decode/projection (pure)
  CommandHistoryWidget.Content.swift    338  CommandHistoryContent + Row + Skeleton (all states)
  CommandHistoryWidget.Previews.swift    73  #Preview per state (Shared-free)
  CommandHistoryWidget.Tests.swift      181  XCTest: format/decode/projection/state/a11y

Web source reproduced: web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/CommandHistoryWidget.tsx
  - STATUS_MAP/DEFAULT_STATUS -> CommandHistoryStatus (feed greys unknown; compact
    folds unknown into "pending") incl. SF Symbols + design-token tints.
  - formatCommandName -> CommandHistoryFormatting.commandName (underscore->space,
    first-letter upper, acronym casing preserved). Verified by unit test.
  - feedItems/lastEntry -> CommandHistoryProjection.feedItems (sort desc, cap 10)
    + compactSummary (list[0], API order). isCompact = size.cols <= 1.
  - WidgetEventFeed/TimelineItem -> CommandHistoryRow (icon, title, status, relative
    time). WidgetShell chrome -> header (title, stale chip, offline chip, refresh).

Data binding (S8, no direct HTTP in the view): CommandHistoryModel binds the shared
  KMP CommandsStore.commandHistory(vehicleId:) StateFlow<Resource<JsonElement>> via
  StateHolderModel + LoadableState.from (mirrors VehicleSettingsModel). JsonElement
  decoded with String(describing:) + JSONDecoder (mirrors SharedLiveStreamProvider).
  refresh() -> store.refreshCommandHistory(vehicleId:). vehicleID==nil -> disabled
  feed (web enabled:!!vehicleId). useVehicles first-vehicle fallback is the host's job.

States rendered (every one): loading (motion-aware skeleton, Reduce-Motion gated),
  content (compact badge OR feed), empty (translation.widget.noCommands), error
  (queryError + retry), stale (TSFreshnessIndicator chip), offline (cached rows +
  wifi.slash chip, or offline empty state + retry). Branch selection is the pure,
  unit-tested CommandHistoryContent.displayMode(for:isCompact:).

i18n (P1/S10): all strings via LocalizedStringKey against Localization/Localizable
  .xcstrings — no English literals. Surface keys (verified present in catalog):
  translation.widget.commandHistory / commandSuccess / commandFailed /
  commandPending / noCommands. Chrome reuses existing keys: translation.commands
  .staleData, translation.common.{offline,refresh,retry,loading},
  translation.queryError.{title,offlineTitle,offlineDetail}.

Telemetry (P1/S11): CommandHistoryModel.onAppear() emits the typed
  Telemetry.track(TelemetryEvent.ScreenView(screen:"CommandHistoryWidget",
  platform:, appVersion:)) once. (The taxonomy is closed — ADR-016 §5 — so the
  contract's typed ScreenView event carries the "view opened" surface slug; no
  free-form "view.opened" string is permitted by the contract.)

Accessibility: feed rows + compact row are single combined VoiceOver elements with
  command+status+time labels; refresh/offline have explicit labels; decorative
  glyphs accessibilityHidden; Dynamic Type via Font.TS ramp; Reduce-Motion gates the
  skeleton pulse.

Registry: id "command-history", category "commands", default 2x4, min 1x2, max 4x40
  (exposed on CommandHistoryWidget.Registry for the dashboard host).

